  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following gas phase dissociation, $\\mathrm{PCl}_5(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{PCl}_3(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\mathrm{~g})$ with equilibrium constant $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{p}}$ at a particular temperature and at pressure $P$. The degree of dissociation $(\\alpha)$ for $\\mathrm{PCl}_5(\\mathrm{~g})$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Voqzd",
      "text": "$\\alpha=\\left(\\frac{K_P}{K_P+P}\\right)^{1 / 3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Liq6Y",
      "text": "$\\alpha=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}+\\mathrm{P}}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qdpyX",
      "text": "$\\alpha=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}+\\mathrm{P}}\\right)^{1 / 2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Ouk5Y",
      "text": "$\\alpha=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}+\\mathrm{P}}\\right)^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{lccc} & \\mathrm{PCl}_5(\\mathrm{g}) &\\rightleftharpoons & \\mathrm{PCl}_3(\\mathrm{g}) & + & \\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\mathrm{g}) \\\\\n\\text{initially} & 1 & & 0 & & 0 \\\\\n\\text{moles taken} & & & \\\\\n\\begin{array}{l} \\text{moles of equilibrium} \\end{array} & 1-\\alpha & & \\alpha & & \\alpha \\\\\n& & &\\end{array}$\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{PC}_3} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{Cl}_2}}{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{PCl}_5}} & \\because \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{gas}} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{T}} \\\\\n\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}\\right)^2}{\\left(\\frac{1-\\alpha}{1+\\alpha} \\cdot \\mathrm{P}\\right)} & \\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{PC}_3}=\\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{Cl}_2}=\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha} \\\\\n\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}=\\frac{\\alpha^2 \\mathrm{P}}{1-\\alpha^2} & \\mathrm{X}_{\\mathrm{PC}_5}=\\frac{1-\\alpha}{1+\\alpha} \\\\\n\\alpha=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{P}}+\\mathrm{P}}\\right)^{1 / 2} & \\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
